{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"Let's evaluate the two sigma expressions and see which of them results in $-\\dfrac{2}{5} -\\dfrac{2}{7}  -\\dfrac{2}{9}  -\\dfrac{2}{11}$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\displaystyle\\sum_{j=1}^4\\left(-\\dfrac{2}{4+j}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\left[-\\dfrac{2}{4+(1)}\\right]+\\left[-\\dfrac{2}{4+(2)}\\right]+\\left[-\\dfrac{2}{4+(3)}\\right]+\\left[-\\dfrac{2}{4+(4)}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-\\dfrac{2}{5} -\\dfrac{1}{3} -\\dfrac{2}{7} -\\dfrac{1}{4}\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\displaystyle\\sum_{j=1}^4\\left(-\\dfrac{2}{2j+3}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\left[-\\dfrac{2}{2(1)+3}\\right]+\\left[-\\dfrac{2}{2(2)+3}\\right]+\\left[-\\dfrac{2}{2(3)+3}\\right]+\\left[-\\dfrac{2}{2(4)+3}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-\\dfrac{2}{5} -\\dfrac{2}{7} -\\dfrac{2}{9} -\\dfrac{2}{11}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, only $\\displaystyle\\sum_{j=1}^4\\left(-\\dfrac{2}{2j+3}\\right)$ is equal to $-\\dfrac{2}{5} -\\dfrac{2}{7} -\\dfrac{2}{9} -\\dfrac{2}{11}$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Consider the sum $-\\dfrac{2}{5}  -\\dfrac{2}{7}  -\\dfrac{2}{9}  -\\dfrac{2}{11}$.\n\n**Which expression is equal to the above sum?**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$\\displaystyle\\sum_{j=1}^4\\left(-\\dfrac{2}{4+j}\\right)$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\displaystyle\\sum_{j=1}^4\\left(-\\dfrac{2}{2j+3}\\right)$","correct":true},{"content":"","isNoneOfTheAbove":true}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":true,"multipleSelect":true,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
